# Kept deliberately as a denylist of things that must never enter the build
# context, not just an optimisation. `docker build` uploads the whole context to
# the daemon, and any later `COPY . .` would bake whatever is present into a
# layer — where it survives even if a subsequent step deletes it.

# Credentials. .env holds the database password; certs/ is where the Supabase CA
# bundle lands.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
certs/
# `**/` is load-bearing: a leading `*.pem` is matched against the path from the
# context root and does not cross `/`, so it would miss `config/server.pem`.
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Reinstalled from the lockfile inside the image; copying the host's copy would
# also ship darwin-native binaries into a linux image.
node_modules

# Built in the builder stage.
dist

.git
.gitignore
**/*.log
npm-debug.log*
**/.DS_Store

# Not part of the runtime image. Excluded from the context rather than relied on
# `tsconfig` to skip: `pnpm run build` would compile them into dist/ otherwise,
# and the fake credentials in pool.test.ts have no business in a shipped layer.
**/*.test.ts
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
OPERATIONS.md
